was amazing to work with Aaron Paul he  is so sweet and loving and just a really  really open warm kind person and just as  an actor is totally willing to be giving  in every single moment and just wants to  give you everything you need and there's  never any sort of wall up he's always  just honest and present and and also  just a really lovely human being to be  around I love him  challenging is kind of a hard word  because to do a film like smashed it was  I would say the most challenging because  it challenged me in so many ways it  challenged me personally and creatively  and emotionally but I wouldn't say that  it was hard I think doing kind of bigger  budget action films and things like that  that I've done that have been you know  shot over the course of six months  sometimes were harder because I had to  really work to keep my stamina up and to  keep the passion going and to be focused  on the character over that long span of  time so for this it was challenging in  so many ways but it was still fun and  kind of effortless as well  Thank You Quentin is just so much fun  he's just kind of the definition of fun  and exuberant exuberance and and joy and  passion for what he does and so I think  that I just learned to really to make  every day count and to make it fun and  to really give to all the people around  you I mean he really is just such a  positive force he loves to just kind of  take people aside and tell them what's  great about them you know just sit down  with a person and say this is why you're  so talented this is why I love you this  is why you're on my movie and I think  just giving that possible positivity on  such a regular basis makes such a  difference sent and I hope to to bring a  little bit of that you know to the job  myself  we even really expect anything from  director what I like in a director is  trust I like to be able to trust the  director and I like to feel that he  trusts me or he or she I'm sorry  trust me and and and so that's that just  makes a really big difference when you  feel that someone can trust your  instincts and isn't going to be afraid  of you doing something different than  what they had in mind that's what it  makes a really nice relationship and it  feels more like a collaboration  I think having worked as a child actor  and just having worked for so long now I  think I never really have to worry about  the discipline of being an actor and the  technical things that come along with it  because I feel like I got that from  training at such a young age you know I  don't really have to make myself sit  down and learn my lines or you know  remember to hit my mark and just show up  on work to work on time and things like  that that all that stuff just sort of  comes naturally to me it's just a part  of who I am and I can really focus on  the creative aspect of it so I'm very  very grateful for that background and  also it kind of reminds me that it is  play because that's what it started out  for me as it wasn't work it was play and  I did it because it was fun I didn't do  it to make money and I try to still have  that that mindset about it that if it  stops being fun then I have to make a  change because there's something about  it that I'm not doing right so I try to  keep that in mind
 

